  "body": "Stacked on #2254. The base is `issue/2238-frame-cost-rule`. Retarget this PR to `main` before #2254 merges.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `boundary_draft::Preview` has a new field `fill` (the triangles of the preview area, `Arc<[[Point2; 3]]>`).\n- `refresh_preview` makes the triangles one time, together with the region. The key does not change: the draft parameters, the draft area, the geometry source and the document version.\n- `world::collect` reads the stored triangles. It does not call `Region::triangles` on each frame now.\n- `boundary_viz::fill_of` makes the triangles inside the span `ui/properties.boundary.preview.triangulate`. `preview_fill` returns the stored triangles.\n- `docs/decisions/2246-area-preview-fill.md`: the decision.\n\nDisplay only. No change to cut geometry, posted G-code or goldens.\n\n## Readings (release, fig8.step, state c of the #2238 probe, ms for each still frame)\n\n| | commands | scene | UI | Total |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| before (#2254) | 0.01 | 18.20 | 11.84 | 30.0 |\n| after | 0.01 | 2.76 | 12.02 | 14.8 |\n\nThe rest of state c is #2247 (chips 4.95, `align_321` 1.96), #2250 (1.13) and #2248 (0.84).\n\n## Tests\n\n- `frame_cost_probe::still_frames_on_fig8_name_their_costs`: in state c, the scene draws the fill on each frame and triangulates 0 times.\n- `frame_cost_probe::area_preview_fill_is_made_once_per_draft` (new):\n  - still frames keep the same triangles (`Arc::ptr_eq`);\n  - a draft change from Outside to Inside gives other triangles;\n  - a change back to Outside gives the first triangles again;\n  - an applied `EditOperationBoundary` and its `Undo` make the triangles again, and they agree with the area.\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: 969 passed, 6 ignored (debug, `-j 6 --test-threads=6`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The real window: GPU upload and present are not measured.\n- A maintainer test build is in `.claude/tmp/test-builds/`, if it is there (see the issue comment).\n\nChangelog: The Boundary group's area preview no longer slows the viewport: its fill is computed once when the area changes.\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2246\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
